<h2>A procedural tangle, untangled</h2>
<div class="flow">
  <div class="fstep"><strong>September 2024.</strong> Status quo ordered in the Section 9 petition — the protective umbrella over the disputed subject matter.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>October 2025.</strong> With an arbitrator appointed, the petition is disposed of to be treated as a Section 17 application before the tribunal.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>2025–2026.</strong> The Supreme Court stays the appointment order; the High Court recalls its disposal order; the Section 9 petition revives; the arbitration freezes.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>4 November 2026.</strong> The SLP is dismissed. The appointment is operative — but the cautious arbitrator defers, awaiting the High Court&rsquo;s word on the still-pending petition.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>25 November 2026.</strong> The High Court clears the track: arbitration proceeds, the petition converts, status quo questions go to the tribunal, and the next hearing date is cancelled.</div>
